(footprint "SX1262-QFN-24-1EP_4x4mm_P0.5mm_EP-vias"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "kicad-footprint-generator")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "SX1262 QFN-24, 4x4mm, 0.5mm pitch, 2.6x2.6mm exposed pad, with five ground vias through the pad. Semtech land pattern SX1261/2 Rev 2.2 Fig 16-3 NOTE 3: thermal vias in the exposed pad SHALL be connected to a system ground plane. At +22 dBm the part dissipates roughly 230 mW, and on a two-layer board the exposed pad is also the radio's entire ground return. Forked from KiCad Package_DFN_QFN:QFN-24-1EP_4x4mm_P0.5mm_EP2.6x2.6mm; vias 0.55/0.3mm in a plus at 0.9mm, tented on the bottom. They are ORDINARY plated through holes, not plugged: JLCPCB's plugged-via rules exclude a via that has a mask opening on either side (the exposed pad's own opening is one) and cap plugged vias at 0.5mm, so paste wicking is controlled at the stencil instead -- keep the window-pane apertures below and do not merge them into one aperture. paste windows moved to (+/-0.72, +/-0.72) 0.82x0.82mm so none overlaps a via barrel.")
	(tags "QFN NoLead SX1262 EP vias")
